    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp19Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation on the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreation.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `\"AUDIT\"`.\n- Reads the authenticated user from `SecurityContextHolder`, and the new owner's `id` and `membershipNumber` from the `@Val Owner` (populated after `SaveOwner` persists it).\n- Emits: `owner created: user={} id={} membershipNumber={}`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (so the owner has its generated id), under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe Cp19 acceptance test confirms the AUDIT logger received `owner created: user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`, satisfying the \"record the authenticated user and the new owner's id and membership number\" requirement.",
